The Chernoff bound actually implies something slightly stronger for the relevant case where η is
close to 0 (i.e., where C works reasonably well), namely that r = O(η log(1/δ)/ε2 ) repetitions suffice. In
particular, if ε is set to a small constant times η, then r = O(log(1/δ)/ε) repetitions suffice rather than
O(log(1/δ)/ε2 ).

